    <string name="liquid_glass_page_touch_summary">Glow, squish, tap buzz and the glass selector</string>
    <string name="liquid_glass_page_notifications_summary">Cards and pop-ups</string>
    <string name="liquid_glass_touch_note">Touch glow shows on Quick Settings tiles. Squish works on glass buttons, cards and tiles. Tap buzz only buzzes where Android doesn\'t already.</string>
    <string name="liquid_glass_melt_summary">Glass merges like drops where it meets, and panels pull away from what opened them on a neck that stretches and snaps. Off to start with: it\'s an extra</string>
    <string name="liquid_glass_motion_note">Morph speed comes on top of Android\'s animation speed, and nothing morphs with animations off. A panel morphs whether or not it\'s glass, as long as the material isn\'t Solid. Each panel has its own switch on its page.</string>
    <string name="liquid_glass_notifications_summary">In the shade, on the lock screen and as pop-up notifications</string>
    <string name="liquid_glass_qs_place_summary">The shade, its tiles and the unlock screen</string>
    <string name="liquid_glass_volume_frosted_summary">Blurs what\'s behind the panel. When off, it follows Glass middle in Edges</string>
    <string name="liquid_glass_clock_use_summary">Shows it on the lock screen in place of your current clock face</string>
    <string name="liquid_glass_clock_faces_summary">Pick any lock screen clock face</string>
    <string name="liquid_glass_clock_note">The wallpaper bends through the Glass clock\'s numbers and their edges catch the light, which follows the phone\'s tilt. It works whether or not glass is on elsewhere. Over a live wallpaper, which the clock can\'t see, the numbers are milky glass.</string>
